# Functional requirements are capabilities

Functional requirements (FR-*) state **what the product must be able to do**. They do not name types, fields, functions, modules, strategy identifiers, or argument lists.

## Split

| Layer | Owns |
| --- | --- |
| **FR** | User-visible capabilities |
| **Baseline / milestones** | Which subset ships in which version |
| **Architecture** | Layers and placement (`docs/design/layers.md`); not a frozen tree |
| **NFR** | Language, tests, RNG, docs |
| **Acceptance** | Concrete checks (`cri == 0` is fine here) |

## Do not put in an FR

- Type or constructor names (`CsiReport`, `CsiConfig`)
- Field or parameter names (`cri`, `W`, `noise_variance`)
- Function signatures (`compute_csi_report(channel, ...)`)
- Module layout or “independent files”
- Strategy slugs (`single_resource`)
- Frozen argument tuples `(seed, n_realizations, snr_grid, config)`
- Implementation recipes (“mask on the same codebook object”, “no-op pass-through interface”)

Those belong in `docs/design/layers.md` or `.cursor/engineering-conventions.md`, not in an FR. Keep FR identifiers stable when rewriting text. See `.cursor/rules/single-home.mdc`.

## Examples

```text
❌ The package must define a CsiReport type with integer fields cri, ri, pmi, cqi, li.
✅ The package must produce a CSI report containing CRI, RI, PMI, CQI, and LI.

❌ Baseline strategy: single_resource → cri = 0.
✅ With a single CSI-RS resource, the reported CRI must be that resource’s index.

❌ Monte Carlo runs must be reproducible from (seed, n_realizations, snr_grid, config).
✅ Monte Carlo results must be reproducible from a documented set of run controls.

❌ Each of FR-10–FR-14 must be an independent module.
✅ CRI, RI, PMI, CQI, and LI selection must each be testable in isolation.
```

When adding a requirement, write the capability first. If a sentence still works after you delete every identifier that would appear in Python, it can stay an FR.
